{"text": "PHILIP MORRIS & CO. LTD., INC.\nINTER-OFFICE ConResPoNDeNce DOG, NO. ZZ\n\nRichmond,\n\nVirginia\n\n\u00a2\nTo: Mr. L. H. Davis Date: September 2, 1952\n\nFrom: FP, A. Hedberg .\nSubject: Progress Report - Period August 16 to 31, 1952.\n\nHave taken 325 samples wugKiu\n\n1. Accomplishments.\n. for calibration of the Tag meter on the-S\u00e9venth floor.\n\n. The comparison of six brands for-Dr. Arkin has been com-\npleted and the results have been sent to him.\n\n2. Activities. The mornings of each day of the past two-week\nperiod were spent on the Seventh Floor taking samples of to~\nbacco before it entered the cooler, for the purpose of cali-\nrating the Tag meter. 325 samples were collected, tested in\nthe Tag meter and in the Freas oven, making a complete total\nof 485 samples taken for this purpose.\n\nThe afternoons of these days were taken up, to a large extent,\n\nwith the routine weight variance calculations and some length\nand soft spot testing of various samples of cigarettes.\n\n3. Plans for Action. The work on the Tag meter will contime,\nalong with routine work in the quality control laboratory.\n\n8PESSZ000z", "words": [{"text": "PHILIP", "x0": 250, "y0": 41, "x1": 301, "y1": 54, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "MORRIS", "x0": 310, "y0": 41, "x1": 374, "y1": 54, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "&", "x0": 383, "y0": 42, "x1": 392, "y1": 54, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "CO.", "x0": 402, "y0": 41, "x1": 430, "y1": 54, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "LTD.,", "x0": 440, "y0": 42, "x1": 476, "y1": 56, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "INC.", "x0": 486, "y0": 42, "x1": 520, "y1": 55, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "INTER-OFFICE", "x0": 216, "y0": 65, "x1": 355, "y1": 75, "conf": 70.0}, {"text": "ConResPoNDeNce", "x0": 369, "y0": 66, "x1": 557, "y1": 77, "conf": 22.0}, {"text": "DOG,", "x0": 611, "y0": 61, "x1": 639, "y1": 79, "conf": 50.0}, {"text": "NO.", "x0": 649, "y0": 60, "x1": 668, "y1": 78, "conf": 15.0}, {"text": "ZZ", "x0": 676, "y0": 50, "x1": 743, "y1": 79, "conf": 52.0}, {"text"